This is a source-available / binary license, not an open-source license.
"The Library" means FlyghtNinno: its headers, precompiled archives, source
code (where provided), web UI, documentation and examples.

1. What you may do (free, with a license key)
   a. Use the Library to develop, build and run firmware for your own or your
      customers' devices, including commercial products.
   b. Distribute firmware binaries that contain the Library, as part of a
      device or product, to end users.
   c. Copy and change the examples for your own sketches.

2. What you may not do
   a. Redistribute, sell, sublicense or publish the Library itself, in whole
      or in part, in source or precompiled form, outside of a firmware binary
      as allowed in 1b (for example: as a library, a fork, a package, a
      repository mirror or a code snippet collection).
   b. Modify the Library and distribute the modified Library.
   c. Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the precompiled archives,
      except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits it.
   d. Use the Library, its API design, web UI or documentation to create a
      competing library, SDK or framework.
   e. Remove, hide or alter copyright notices, license notices or the
      "Built with FlyghtNinno" attribution, except through the White label
      feature where your edition allows it.
   f. Bypass, disable, patch or tamper with the license key check, forge or
      alter license keys, or share your license key with anyone outside your
      organisation, other than inside firmware binaries as allowed in 1b.

3. License keys and editions
   Using the Library requires a license key (API_KEY) issued by the copyright
   holder. Free keys are available at no cost; Pro and Enterprise keys come
   with a separate commercial license. A key is personal to its licensee,
   whose name it carries, and covers the releases published up to the update
   date it states. Without a valid key the Library runs in a time-limited
   evaluation mode, which may be used for evaluation and testing only and
   not in a product. Keys that leak or are misused may be revoked.

4. Third-party components
   Components listed in NOTICE stay under their own licenses.

5. Termination
   This license ends automatically if you break its terms. Firmware already
   delivered to end users before termination may continue to be used by them.

